{
  "uid": "dailies-observability",
  "title": "Dailies - render pipeline and the agent watching it",
  "description": "Two halves, which is the point. The left half is the render farm; the right half is the Gemini agent that reads it. An agent that watches a pipeline is itself a pipeline, and one that cannot be observed is one nobody can trust with a deadline.",
  "tags": [
    "dailies",
    "render",
    "gen-ai",
    "agentic-cinema"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-24h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "1m",
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Render pipeline health",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "bargauge",
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Frames completed vs expected, by shot",
      "description": "The pair that defines this project's failure: a shot can read complete on both numbers and still have produced a broken frame, which is why the board carries a second opinion the metrics cannot give. Aggregated with max by (shot) because a re-rendered shot emits one series per execution, and the bare metric drew the same shot twice as if two different things had happened.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 9,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": "max by (shot) (last_over_time(render_job_frames_completed_total[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{shot}} done",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": "max by (shot) (last_over_time(render_job_frames_expected[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{shot}} expected",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "basic",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "min": 0,
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Frame render duration",
      "description": "Reconstructed from the histogram buckets rather than sum/count: identical durations give a sum/count spread of zero, which reads as high confidence when it is really a sample of one.\n\nA stat rather than a timeseries, and that choice decides the query. As a timeseries every point used the same whole-window lookback, so it drew a perfectly flat line carrying nothing the number does not. A stat issues an INSTANT query, and instant is where increase() breaks here: a render is a short-lived job with one sample per series, so increase has nothing to extrapolate from and returns NaN. Measured: the same expression gives NaN instant and 689 points over a range.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 9,
        "x": 9,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (last_over_time(render_frame_duration_seconds_bucket[$__range])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (last_over_time(render_frame_duration_seconds_bucket[$__range])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "#7fe3ff"
          },
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bargauge",
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Peak worker memory, by render job",
      "description": "The failure a render farm already catches, kept beside the ones it does not so the contrast is visible.\n\nLabelled by render job and worker, not by shot: render_worker_memory_bytes carries no shot label at all. The panel used to claim one, so Grafana fell back to printing the entire series name and the legend was unreadable.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": "last_over_time(render_worker_memory_bytes[$__range])",
          "legendFormat": "{{render_job}} \u00b7 {{worker}}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "lcd",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "color": {
            "mode": "continuous-BlPu"
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Agent health - the half that observes the observer",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "bargauge",
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Gemini tokens by type",
      "description": "Thinking tokens are billed and invisible in the answer, so an agent whose cost is only counted at the output underreports itself several times over.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 9,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (gen_ai_token_type) (last_over_time(gen_ai_client_token_usage_sum[$__range]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{gen_ai_token_type}}",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "continuous-YlBl"
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Investigation latency (p95)",
      "description": "One press of Diagnose is several sequential Grafana queries plus a Gemini call, so this is the number a supervisor actually waits through. increase() rather than last_over_time() because Cloud Run replaces the instance on every deploy and resets the counter; the bare last value described only the newest process. It works here and not for the render metrics because the API is a long-lived service with many samples per series.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 7,
        "x": 9,
        "y": 11
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (increase(gen_ai_client_operation_duration_seconds_bucket[$__range])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#ffb020",
                "value": 45
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Investigations run",
      "description": "Every one of these is a Vertex call somebody paid for, which is why the public Diagnose route carries a per-shot cooldown.\n\nCounted with increase() across instance restarts. last_over_time() reported 1 while the true figure for the same window was 17: each deploy starts a fresh process whose counter begins at zero, and the last value is only ever the newest one's.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 11
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "grafanacloud-prom"
          },
          "expr": "round(sum(increase(gen_ai_client_operation_duration_seconds_count[$__range])))",
          "legendFormat": "investigations",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "fixed",
            "fixedColor": "#7fe3ff"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    }
  ]
}
